## A Disturbing Trend in Food Recalls

So far in 2026, the food industry has issued 500 recalls. Out of these, a staggering 152 were linked to Salmonella contamination, making it the leader in food safety issues. Compare this to the next largest category, undeclared allergens, at 246 recalls this year, and the disparity is stark.

### The salmonella saga continues

Salmonella has been a consistent issue, and recent data suggests its proliferation is still a major concern. On May 27th, 2026, six recalls were announced for products potentially contaminated with Salmonella. These products included trail mixes, seasonings, and powdered flavors. Ghirardelli Chocolate Company, a well-known brand, is among the culprits, recalling its Sweet Ground Powder White Chocolate Flavored and Perfectly Premium Frappe Mix Frozen Hot Cocoa for possible Salmonella contamination. Solina U.S. Holding also issued recalls for bulk seasoning products due to the same concern.

### Repeat offenders: a persistent problem

Interestingly, some brands appear on recall lists more frequently than others. For instance, Moonlight Packing Corporation and Albertsons Companies LLC are among the top offenders, with each issuing 11 recalls (mostly Class I) this year. Ghirardelli Chocolate Company also made headlines as a repeat violator, with 10 recalls so far in 2026.

### The verdict

Manufacturers must prioritize preventive measures and supply chain transparency. The recurrence of similar issues suggests systemic flaws that need immediate attention. Regulators should tighten oversight, and brands must take responsibility for their role in ensuring food safety.
